  "body": "## What changed\n\n`rotary_dflat::a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement` has been red on main since #223 (bisected: `c9a9fb3^1` passes): the through-flat bar read \"the model's normals share no rotation axis\".\n\n**Cause.** #223 rightly stopped an off-axis boss lending its bearings: the coarseness gate (and the point-share rule's pencil skip) read only facets whose normal lines meet the axis within the concurrency tolerance. A D-flat's facets miss that line by part of the flat's width (0.2-0.4 mm on this bar, tol 0.18), so they were set aside too - and a single-band D-flat bar is one wall pencil with a ~39 degree skip at the flat (0.69 rad vs the 0.49 budget).\n\n**Fix** (`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/axis_point.rs`, `axis.rs`):\n\n- `faces_axis(d, ax)`: a facet square to the axis (`|n . u| < 0.05`) whose centroid's normal line misses it by less than half the facet's own size (`sqrt(area) / 2`) faces the axis - the axis's foot falls on the face.\n- Its normal now counts in `judge`'s coarseness gate and in `borne_out`'s point-share pencil skip.\n- A boss's facets miss the part's axis by its offset (millimetres), far more than half their size, so they still lend nothing - every #208 / #223 boss and prism pin stays green.\n- Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#246).\n\nNote: PR #247 (#237) also edits `axis_point.rs`, in a different function (`borne_out`'s fold check / new `folded`); whichever merges second takes a trivial merge.\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, current main)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --tests`: `rotary_dflat` 4/4 (red on main); only `swarf_pose_continuity` x2 fails (known on main).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --tests`: only `drilling_axial::a_drill_where_the_model_has_no_hole_is_convicted` fails (known on main).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `multiaxis::axis_point::tests::a_single_band_d_flat_bar_reads_its_axis` - four flat azimuths read Z (fails on main with \"share no rotation axis\").\n- `rotary_dflat::a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement` (back to green).\n\nChangelog: A single-band bar with a D-flat fits its axis again (regressed in the point-concurrency guard)\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork).\n\nFixes #246\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
